; claude: a small JavaScript: Js_lexer (the text to tokens), Js_ast (the
; tree), Js_parse (statements by recursive descent, expressions by Pratt
; -- and why not yacc), Js_value (values, objects, the conversions),
; Js_eval (the tree walked: scopes, closures, this, the errors) and
; Js_builtins (console, Math, strings' and arrays' methods). The
; language only: what a script can touch outside itself is its host's,
; a record of functions, so the browser gives it a page
; (src/browser/Browser_script) and a test gives it nothing.
;
; Pure OCaml, no Playground; the modules are Js_ because the libraries
; are unwrapped and js_of_ocaml's own module is Js.
(library
 (name javascript)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries tiny_libs.random) ; Lehmer, Math.random's seeded numbers
)
